# L §3.2 Inline figures: "a bare literal in a row or a pin takes its target's declared type and unit (`with
# net_loss[b] = 2000` on a `money USD` def is 2 000.00 USD, never a year)".  L §8.2: the pin is listed.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2027-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

source s "s"
unit USD: currency minor 0.01
index bs = [b1, b2]
input loss[b in bs]: money USD
def net_loss[b in bs]: money USD = loss[b] at reader

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  loss[b1] = 1.00
  loss[b2] = 3.00

ask q1: net_loss[b1] + net_loss[b2] with net_loss[b1] = 2000 law 2026-12-31
=== expect
q1: 2 003.00 USD
  pinned: net_loss[b1] = 2 000.00 USD
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2027-01-01
